This benchmark adapts the FP32 inference algorithm and HIP kernels from:
https://github.com/Uzair-90/llama-inference-hip
Local source: llama-inference-hip-main (unversioned source snapshot).
That project carries the GNU General Public License version 3, reproduced in LICENSE.
It credits Andrej Karpathy's llama2.c: https://github.com/karpathy/llama2.c.

The adapted benchmark files in this directory and samples/llama are distributed
under GPL-3.0-only. The surrounding MGPUSim source retains its existing license.
No model weights or tokenizer data are bundled.

Changes: Go checkpoint loader and host orchestration; OpenCL kernel adaptation;
static local scratch arrays; barrier before reusing max-reduction scratch;
CPU verification, deterministic synthetic fixture, and benchmark runner.

The embedded kernel binary links AMD ROCm device libraries 5.0.0.
Their notices and redistribution terms are reproduced in ROCM-DEVICE-LIBS-LICENSE.
